const sentence = (text) => esc(text).replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>')
const start = `<section class="start" aria-labelledby="start"><h2 id="start">Start a project</h2><p><code>npx openquarry init</code> starts a folder of notes or a course, and <code>npx openquarry check</code> validates its frontmatter and manifests. Both are commands of the <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/openquarry"><code>openquarry</code></a> package.</p>${beforeRelease ? `<div class="callout before-release"><p>${sentence(beforeRelease.text)}</p></div>` : ''}${starters.map((s) => `<h3 id="start-${s.id}">${s.title}</h3><p>${s.text}</p>${codeBlock(initCommands(s), 'bash')}`).join('')}<h3 id="start-check">Check a project</h3><p><code>check</code> prints one line for each file it checks and lists any errors under it. It exits with 1 when a file is invalid, which fails a CI job.</p>${codeBlock(checkCommand, 'bash')}<h3 id="start-new">Add a note or a lesson</h3><p><code>new</code> writes a Markdown file with a new <code>id</code>, a <code>slug</code> made from the title, <code>version: 1.0.0</code> and its <code>contentType</code>.</p>${codeBlock(newCommands.notes, 'bash')}${codeBlock(newCommands.course, 'bash')}<h3 id="start-id">Print a new id</h3><p>A note or a lesson written by hand needs its own <code>id</code>, and this command prints a new UUID.</p>${codeBlock(idCommand, 'bash')}<p>The command needs Node 18 or later. <code>init</code> copies a starter that ships inside the package, so it works offline. It refuses a folder that already holds files unless you pass <code>--force</code>, and it never overwrites a file. <a href="${repo}/tree/master/packages/openquarry#readme">The package's README</a> describes every option.</p><h3 id="start-degit">Copy a starter with degit</h3><p>degit copies the same two starters straight from GitHub. Each starter's <code>check</code> script validates its files with <code>@framers/openquarry</code>.</p>${starters.map((s) => codeBlock(startCommands(s), 'bash', s.title)).join('')}<p>The degit commands need Node 20 or later. <code>npx degit</code> copies the starter's folder from GitHub without its history.</p><ul><li><a href="${repo}/tree/master/templates">The starters on GitHub</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/framerslab/openquarry/tree/master/examples/reading-a-map">The example course</a>, Reading a map: two units of lessons and exercises, an assessment and a catalogue</li><li><a href="/schema/">The schemas</a></li><li><a href="${commandNpm}">openquarry on npm</a>, <a href="${npm}">@framers/openquarry on npm</a> and <a href="${repo}">the source on GitHub</a></li></ul></section>`

